' 01 - HELLO WORLD
'
' Every program here is an Ilwaco project. Open the .vfp, press Build, then Run.
'
' A line starting with an apostrophe is a COMMENT. FreeBASIC ignores it
' completely; comments are notes for the person reading the code -- often you,
' six months later.

' PRINT writes a line to the console.
Print "Hello, world!"

' A string is text in double quotes. Print with no argument leaves a blank line.
Print
Print "This program was built with Ilwaco IDE."

' Several values on one line: separate them with a semicolon. The semicolon
' joins them with no space, so put spaces inside the strings where you want them.
Print "Two"; " "; "words"

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Keeps the window open so you can read the output. Sleep with no argument
' waits for a keypress.
Print
Print "Press any key to close..."
Sleep
